{"title":"Quantitative Analyst Roadmap","role":"Quantitative Analyst","summary":"A Quantitative Analyst (Quant) uses mathematics, statistics, programming, and financial theory to analyze markets, price financial instruments, manage risk, optimize portfolios, and develop systematic trading or investment models.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Mathematics & Computing"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Quantitative Analyst (Quant) uses mathematics, statistics, programming, and financial theory to analyze markets, price financial instruments, manage risk, optimize portfolios, and develop systematic trading or investment models."},{"type":"p","text":"Mathematics & Computing is one of the stronger undergraduate foundations for quantitative finance because it combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced mathematics"},{"text":"Probability and statistics"},{"text":"Algorithms"},{"text":"Programming"},{"text":"Numerical methods"},{"text":"Optimization"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Machine learning"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical quant careers include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Quantitative Analyst"},{"text":"Quantitative Researcher"},{"text":"Quantitative Developer"},{"text":"Risk Quant"},{"text":"Algorithmic Trading Analyst"},{"text":"Portfolio Quant"},{"text":"Derivatives Analyst"},{"text":"Financial Data Scientist"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The field is highly competitive. For top quantitative research and trading roles, exceptional mathematical ability, competitive programming/problem solving, probability, statistics, and strong programming matter more than simply having a finance degree or collecting finance certifications."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Area","Potential Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Quantitative Research"},{"text":"Quant Researcher"}],[{"text":"Trading"},{"text":"